# Keep MAME patch files LF-only regardless of core.autocrlf.
#
# `git apply` normalizes the (CRLF) working-tree target to LF internally and
# then expects an LF patch. On Windows / GitHub with core.autocrlf=true a
# checkout would otherwise reintroduce CRLF into these *.patch files, making
# every hunk fail ("patch does not apply") and forcing build_hunter_from_release.sh
# to fall back to `patch -p1`. Pinning them to LF keeps `git apply` working.
*.patch text eol=lf
